   "sig": "A2r-A3v",
   "kind": "paratext",
   "replaces": "",
   "squares": [],
   "es": "POR quanto por parte de vos Alonso de Barros, nuestro criado, nos ha sido hecha relacion, que vos aueys compuesto vna pintura intitulada Filosofia Cortesana, con ciertas differencias de figuras y letras que se contiene en un pliego grande, y la aueys moralizado en vna relacion a parte[.?] Y nos suplicastes, que teniendo consideracion a lo que en ello aueys trabajado, os diessemos licencia, y ma[n]dassemos que vos, o la persona, ò personas que vuestro poder huuieren, lo pedays[?] imprimir, y ve[n]der enestos nuestros reynos, y no otras algunas, o como la nuestra merced fuesse: Y porque auiendose visto por nuestro mandado, parecio ser obra de mucho ingenio, y que serà vtil à la Republica, por ser de honesto y gustoso entretenimiento. Por la presente os damos licencia y facultad, para que por tiempo de diez años primeros siguientes, contados desde el dia de la fecha desta nuestra cedula en adelante, vos a la persona, o personas, que para ello vuestro poder huuieren, podays imprimir y ve[n]der enestos nuestros Reynos y señorios la dicha pintura, y moralidad della. Y ma[n]damos, que otras personas algunas no lo puedan imprimir, ni vender, ni imprima[·] , ni vendan enestos dichos nuestros reynos y señorios, so pena que qualesquier personas que sin tener el dicho vuestro poder lo imprimieren, o hizieren imprimir, o lo vendieren, o hizieren vender, pierdan toda la impression que hizieren i vendieren, i los moldes y aparejos con que lo hizieren, i mas incurran por cada vez en pena de cinquenta mil marauedis. La tercia parte para nuestra camara. Y la tercia parte para el Iuez que lo sentenciare. Y la otra tercia parte para el denunciador. Y mandamos, que cada pliego de la dicha pintura con la dicha moralidad, se venda al precio que por los del nuestro Consejo fuere tassado. A los quales, y a los Presidentes, y Oydores de las nuestras audiencias, y a otros qualesquier juezes y justicias destos dichos nuestros Reynos y señorios, mandamos assimismo, que guarden y cumplan, y hagan guardar y cumplir esta nuestra cedula, y lo en ella contenido. Fecha en Madrid a nueue de Febrero, de mil y quinientos y ochenta y siete años.",
   "en": "Whereas, on behalf of you, Alonso de Barros, our servant, report has been made to us that you have composed a picture entitled <em>Filosofía cortesana</em>, with certain various figures and verses, which is contained on one large sheet, and that you have written a moral explanation of it in a separate account; and you begged us that, taking into consideration the labour you have put into it, we should give you licence, and order that you, or the person or persons holding your power of attorney, might print and sell it in these our kingdoms, and no others whatever, or as our pleasure might be. And because, having been examined by our order, it appeared to be a work of great ingenuity, and one that will be useful to the commonwealth, being honest and pleasant entertainment: by these presents we give you licence and authority so that, for the term of the ten years next following, counted from the day of the date of this our warrant onward, you or the person or persons holding your power for it may print and sell in these our kingdoms and lordships the said picture, and its moral explanation. And we order that no other persons whatever may print it or sell it, nor print nor sell it in these our said kingdoms and lordships, on pain that any persons who, without holding your said power, should print it or cause it to be printed, or sell it or cause it to be sold, shall lose the whole impression that they make and sell, and the formes and equipment with which they make it, and shall further incur, for each offence, a penalty of fifty thousand maravedís. One third for our Chamber. And one third for the judge who passes sentence. And the other third for the informer. And we order that each sheet of the said picture, with the said moral explanation, be sold at the price that shall be set by those of our Council. To whom, and to the Presidents and Judges (<em>oidores</em>) of our Audiencias, and to any other judges and officers of justice whatever of these our said kingdoms and lordships, we likewise order that they keep and fulfil, and cause to be kept and fulfilled, this our warrant and what it contains. Given in Madrid on the ninth of February, in the year one thousand five hundred and eighty-seven.",
   "note": "(1) <em>Pintura</em> is the printed board, \"one large sheet\" (<em>pliego grande</em>); the <em>relacion a parte</em> / <em>moralidad</em> is this book. The privilege licenses both, and prices them together \"each sheet of the said picture with the said moral explanation\". <em>Letras</em> here are the inscriptions/verses on the board. (2) <em>lo pedays[?] imprimir</em> is rendered as <em>podays</em> (\"might print\"); the transcription notes the e may be an ink-filled o. (3) <em>vos a la persona</em> (pdf 10) is rendered \"you or the person\": the printed a is probably an ink-filled o, and the parallel formula on pdf 9 has <em>o</em>. (4) <em>ni imprima[·] , ni vendan</em>: the n (or tilde) of <em>impriman</em> failed to print; the doubled \"print … sell … nor print nor sell\" is the legal formula, kept. (5) <em>moldes y aparejos</em>: the type set up in formes, and the press equipment. (6) <em>nuestra camara</em>: the royal treasury (the Cámara). <em>Consejo</em>: the royal Council, which set the official price (<em>tasa</em>) per sheet. <em>Oydores</em>: the judges of the Audiencias, the high courts. (7) <em>Cedula</em>: a royal warrant (<em>cédula</em>). The maravedí was the Castilian money of account.",
   "lit": "",
   "vid": ""
