   "es": "Lau Deo.",
   "en": "Praise be to God.",
   "note": "Wilson reads \"Laus Deo.\" on D12v <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"about.html#bib-wilsonCervantesItemEmmanuel1968\" data-key=\"wilsonCervantesItemEmmanuel1968\">Wilson 1968, 365</a>)</span>; the corpus \"Lau\" is a slip. C has the same formula (\"LAVS DEO.\", pdf 69). G closes instead with \"Deo gratias\" (\"Thanks be to God\") <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"about.html#bib-sanchezEdicionesAntiguasFilosofia2016oct16\" data-key=\"sanchezEdicionesAntiguasFilosofia2016oct16\">Lucero Sánchez 2016, 189</a>)</span>.",
   "lit": "",
